Bash Notes
Finally Scripting
--------------------

for loop:
for thing in item1 item2 item3; do
	echo "The item is currently $thing"
done


Syntax check a file without executing it:

bash -n script

no error messages printed to the screen is good

Checking exit code for syntax errors:

ehco $?

if it returns 0 it is a success.
If it returns non-0 there is a syntax error.
